# Accepted CVEs — the visible risk register for image scanning.
# Every entry needs: CVE id, image, reason, review-by date.
# Gate policy: CRITICAL + --ignore-unfixed (unfixable OS-package CVEs are
# visible in the SBOM artifacts but do not fail CI — nothing actionable).

# pgvector/pgvector:pg16 — Go stdlib crypto/tls in the bundled gosu binary.
# gosu runs once at container init to drop root->postgres and makes no TLS
# connections; the vulnerable code path is unreachable. Upstream pg16 tag has
# not rebuilt (digest identical to our pin). Review: next pgvector image bump
# or 2026-12-01, whichever first.
CVE-2025-68121

# pgvector/pgvector:pg16 — perl 5.36 in the Debian bookworm base (libperl5.36,
# perl, perl-base, perl-modules): regex heap overflow / incorrect regex
# processing / Archive::Tar path traversal. Fixed in deb12u4, but the upstream
# pg16 (= pg16-bookworm) tag has NOT been rebuilt (digest 7b822b0a still
# ships deb12u3, scanned 2026-10-18). perl is present only as the plperl
# runtime; nothing in this deployment creates plperl functions and the
# database is reachable solely from litellm / open-webui / rag-api over the
# CNP. The clean alternative, pg16-trixie, changes the glibc/collation base
# and needs a planned REINDEX window — tracked as maintenance, not a CVE fix.
# Review: next pgvector pg16 rebuild or 2026-11-15, whichever first.
CVE-2026-13221
CVE-2026-8376
CVE-2026-42496

# ghcr.io/open-webui/open-webui:v0.12.3 — three library CVEs whose
# preconditions this deployment does not meet (verified against the v0.12.3
# source, 2026-10-18):
#  * PyJWT CVE-2026-102268 (HS/asymmetric confusion when ONE decode allow-list
#    mixes HMAC with an asymmetric alg + raw-PEM key): Open WebUI never mixes
#    — session tokens HS256 only (utils/auth.py), OIDC logout tokens RS*/ES*
#    only (utils/oauth.py), apps tokens EdDSA only (socket/apps.py).
#  * sentence-transformers CVE-2026-68770 (code exec when loading a LOCAL
#    model directory): RAG_EMBEDDING_ENGINE=openai routes embeddings to the
#    gateway; OFFLINE_MODE; no local model dir exists or can be written.
#  * unstructured CVE-2026-71428 (SSRF via partition(url=)): Open WebUI calls
#    unstructured only through file-path loaders (rst/xml/epub); URL fetching
#    uses its own _SSRFSafeAdapter loader; the namespace is egress-locked to
#    litellm/postgres/DNS by CNP.
# Review: next open-webui release that bumps PyJWT>=2.14, unstructured>=0.24,
# sentence-transformers>=5.6 — or 2026-11-15, whichever first.
CVE-2026-102268
CVE-2026-68770
CVE-2026-71428

# (previous entries: 4 open-webui RAG-lib CVEs — nltk RCE x3 CVE-2026-78683/
# 79657/79675, unstructured SSRF CVE-2026-71428 — REMOVED 2026-09-13: the
# v0.11.3 release build ships the fixed versions; pin bumped, scan clean.)
